From 6c17a0458a8ffad7ebf9e773949a3ca2f19cdbda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 17:55:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifipro: read the wireless settings in one call instead of
 116

The page embedded 116 separate server-side nvram evaluations - 29 fields across a
hardcoded wl0..wl3 - and made no client-side calls at all, so every one of them
had to complete before a byte of the page could render. No other page here uses
more than 13. On a tri-band model 29 of the 116 read a wl3 radio that does not
exist.

Replaced with a single call that returns the whole set for the radios this model
actually has. The page's only reader already treated a missing key as empty, and
radios are enumerated from the router's own band list rather than a fixed range,
so absent units being absent is a no-op.
---
 release/src/router/www/Reaper_WiFiPro.asp | 12 +++++-------
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/release/src/router/www/Reaper_WiFiPro.asp b/release/src/router/www/Reaper_WiFiPro.asp
index a5c5551e4c..69c083ce1e 100644
--- a/release/src/router/www/Reaper_WiFiPro.asp
+++ b/release/src/router/www/Reaper_WiFiPro.asp
@@ -161,13 +161,11 @@ code{font-family:ui-monospace,Consolas,monospace}
          ('2'=2.4GHz, '1'=5GHz, '4'=6GHz), in wl_ifnames order. Length = radio count.
          3 on RT-BE96U, 4 on GT-BE98 (dual 5GHz). ---- */
   var NBAND = JSON.parse("<% wl_nband_info(); %>".replace(/'/g,'"'));
-  /* current nvram value for every wlN_field this page can touch, wl0..wl3 (absent units = "") */
-  var NV = {
